WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:02.930
- Okay okay okay.

00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:05.900
This is going to piss some people off.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:08.400
Some of you are going to turn
your backs on me forever,

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:09.400
sorry to see you go.

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:12.280
I have to tell you this reality.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:16.060
I have not shampooed
my hair for five years.

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:18.490
And yet those five years have been

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:21.550
some of the best five
years of my hair's life.

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:24.580
No more itching, no more oily hair,

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:26.740
no more dandruff flakes,

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:30.280
just normal hair that does
weird stuff sometimes,

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.500
but is generally happy.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:33.343
Let me explain.

00:00:35.867 --> 00:00:36.700
Go ahead, take a good look,

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:38.366
I know everyone's already doing
it anyway, look at my hair.

00:00:38.366 --> 00:00:40.030
I've never felt so conscious about my hair

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:41.510
because I'm talking about it.

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:42.970
Okay, so five years ago

00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:45.660
I realized that I was in a cycle.

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:47.190
The cycle looked like this.

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:51.010
My head, which produces
natural protective oils

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:52.610
would be washed with shampoo.

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:55.180
Shampoo is just a chemical that attaches

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:56.900
to these oils on your scalp,

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:58.380
and then when you wash that shampoo out

00:00:58.380 --> 00:00:59.430
the oils are attached to them

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:02.240
and they leave, ridding your head of oils.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:03.940
The shampoo also cleans off any pollen

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:05.190
or dust that's caught in your hair.

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:07.850
So my hair was now clean, very clean.

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:09.040
Oh yeah and this guy isn't me,

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:10.280
this is just a stock footage

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:12.730
representation of me five years ago.

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:14.850
Anyway, then goes in the conditioner,

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:18.240
which coats your hair
with silicone material

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:19.490
that makes it shine,

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:21.970
and restores all of
that shine that was lost

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:24.110
from stripping away all of those oils.

00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:26.890
Man, I haven't used
conditioner in a very long time

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:28.950
but I do remember that it makes your hair

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:32.600
feel like silky butter.

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:34.220
Silky butter, is that even a thing?

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:36.010
Okay, so you strip away the oils,

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:38.620
you coat it with this
shiny silky conditioner,

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:39.780
and then my hair would end up

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:41.490
just being sort of like a fluff ball.

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:43.840
In order to style it I
would put in some product,

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:45.700
like some fancy pomade I bought

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:47.730
at some fancy barber in Chicago.

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:51.590
This pomade is made of, wait for it, oil.

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:53.210
It is an oil based product.

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:54.780
So I'm putting oil back in my hair

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:56.110
after I just stripped it all out.

00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:59.460
Meanwhile, my scalp is like
whoa whoa whoa whoa whoa,

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:01.810
dude you just stripped away
all this protective oil

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:04.330
that we make to protect your scalp, wtf.

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:07.530
And so it fires up it's
natural oil making machine

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:09.280
to produce more oil for your hair.

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:10.720
So now you have double oil,

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:12.680
you've got the pomade
and the natural oils.

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:14.810
So now by the end of the day

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:18.380
you start you feel like
your hair is super oily

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:20.730
and greasy and you have all these messages

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:23.280
about dirty hair being greasy and oily.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:24.980
- You have got greasy hair though bro.

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:25.813
- Aw come on man.

00:02:25.813 --> 00:02:29.120
- So what's the cure for
this oily greasy hair?

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:30.190
Shampoo.

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:31.530
- A deep cleansing shampoo.

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:33.610
It helps take away the
excess dirt and oils

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:34.700
that can be inside your hear.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:36.100
Right, I reckon we should give it a go

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:36.933
and get you washed up.

00:02:36.933 --> 00:02:38.223
- Let's do it.

00:02:38.223 --> 00:02:39.360
- And the whole cycle starts over again.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:41.210
In my mid-20s I also started to realize

00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:44.320
that my scalp was starting to
become like itchy and flaky

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:47.840
which is so embarrassing,
so uncomfortable,

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:50.320
and yet luckily out there in the world

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:51.720
there is a cure for this.

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:53.370
- [Narrator] The problem
of flaking dandruff

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:54.960
can be solved

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:57.300
with just regular use
of Proctor &amp; Gamble's

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:59.870
new wonder shampoo, head and shoulders.

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:02.130
- Okay, listen, just a quick moment

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:05.090
to make it clear that this cycle

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:07.070
is my hair experience.

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:10.760
Which is based on not only
my physiology and genetics,

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:13.200
but also on my standards

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:14.750
and relationship to society

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:16.900
and what society tells
me to do with my hair.

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:18.130
So just to get this out of the way,

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:20.220
I'm not here to preach
what's right for your scalp,

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:23.650
I'm simply telling you
what's right for my scalp.

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:25.780
In fact there's this whole movement,

00:03:25.780 --> 00:03:28.540
sort of a political
movement around shampoo

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:30.670
and not shampooing, it's called no poo

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:34.530
which is a very unfortunate
name for this movement.

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:36.380
I'm not a part of that
movement, I'm not pushing that.

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:37.700
This isn't political for me,

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:39.300
I just want to tell you a story

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:40.590
about the journey of my hair

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:44.370
using a little bit of history
and data and research,

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:47.220
and again most importantly,
my own experience

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:49.370
of five years of not shampooing my hair.

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:50.530
Okay, so let's dive in.

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.100
Let's get some context here.

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:55.400
Human beings used to not wash their hair

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:56.500
very much at all.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:59.120
It was only by the 1970s when ads

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:01.320
targeted mainly towards white women

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:04.530
would come out saying you
need to wash your hair

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:06.030
every single day,

00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:10.008
and that the dirt in your
hair was weighing it down.

00:04:10.008 --> 00:04:11.920
- That attract dirt and
weigh hair down like this.

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:14.660
- And that in order to
prevent this weighing down

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:16.620
and to get body,

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:18.460
you would have to use this product.

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:20.740
This also started a whole
new set of messaging

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:23.140
around greasy hair, dirty hair,

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:25.180
which even saying it is like repulsive.

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:27.720
So demonizing the idea of greasy hair

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:30.660
and pushing this daily shampoo regiment

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:33.050
was seen as the only way to fight back

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:35.310
against this greasy hair epidemic.

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:38.048
Today, Americans wash their hair

00:04:38.048 --> 00:04:40.960
around five of the seven days of the week.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:42.190
By the way that's about double

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:43.910
how much they was their hair on average

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:45.710
in Spain and Italy.

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:48.450
And it's way more than the once a month

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:51.840
Americans used to wash
their hair in the '30s.

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:54.060
So let me tell you the story
of how this all went down,

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:56.590
because I didn't grow
up as a non-shampooer.

00:04:56.590 --> 00:04:59.630
Five years ago I had bought
this really expensive

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:02.650
fancy tea tree oil based dandruff shampoo,

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:06.070
because I had so much itchiness
and flakiness everywhere.

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:07.300
I was so tired of that,

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:08.970
and I was so embarrassed by it.

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:10.100
So I was diligent.

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:12.270
I would wash my hair with this

00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:14.570
tea tree oil shampoo every day.

00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:15.690
The marketing on this told me

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:17.310
that I shouldn't use any other shampoos,

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:19.000
that all the other
shampoos were the devil,

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.990
and that this was the
only thing I could use

00:05:20.990 --> 00:05:22.490
to treat my dandruff.

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:24.080
I ran out of this shampoo

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:25.240
while we were on like a trip,

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:26.690
so I couldn't order it.

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:28.140
And I was just like okay when I get back

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:30.030
I'll order the shampoo
and I'll get back onto it.

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:32.490
And it took a while, we
were on some long trip,

00:05:32.490 --> 00:05:35.300
I get back, I forget to order the shampoo,

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:37.080
I was getting worried about this.

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:39.350
But soon, after like three weeks

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:42.100
of this sort of fear
of using other shampoos

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:44.730
I noticed that the itching
started going away.

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:46.750
and that the greasy hair feel

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:48.570
started to actually level out.

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:50.870
It was actually okay,
and I was secretly like

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:51.830
oh I'm probably,

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.450
I probably just got
used to it or something.

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:54.760
But the key moment happened

00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:56.270
when I went in to get a haircut

00:05:56.270 --> 00:05:59.240
having not washed my hair
with shampoo for like a month.

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:01.360
I was actually really
nervous and conscious

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:02.990
of what the barber was gonna say to me,

00:06:02.990 --> 00:06:04.190
and he didn't say anything.

00:06:04.190 --> 00:06:05.810
So I asked him, I was like hey

00:06:05.810 --> 00:06:08.140
how does my hair and scalp look to you?

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:10.360
And he was like looks
good, it's a little dry,

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:11.680
but overall pretty healthy,

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:13.170
and that was the moment for me.

00:06:13.170 --> 00:06:14.600
I was like wait what?

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:18.220
This guy who sees like
dozens of scalps every day,

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:20.110
dozens of scalps, that's
actually really gross,

00:06:20.110 --> 00:06:21.880
like dozens of scalps,

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:23.210
I'm just never gonna say that again.

00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:25.200
This guy sees a lot of scalps every day

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:28.057
and he blessed my unshampooed scalp,

00:06:28.057 --> 00:06:29.840
and was like you're actually okay.

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:30.990
Now let me just remind you

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:34.080
that I've told some of my
close friends this story before

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:35.120
and they have tried it

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:36.520
and it hasn't worked for them.

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:38.510
I'm not saying that this exact thing

00:06:38.510 --> 00:06:39.730
is going to work for you.

00:06:39.730 --> 00:06:41.430
The reason I am making this video

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:44.460
is because I want us to
have reasons to be skeptical

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:46.970
of all the messages that we get fed

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:48.530
around this topic.

00:06:48.530 --> 00:06:50.940
- [Narrator] Nourishing damaged
hair back to healthy life.

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:52.250
- Regular washing is the only way

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:53.980
that you can get rid of that excess oils.

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:55.380
- I feel no grease.

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:57.590
- A few years ago I read
this kind of obnoxious

00:06:57.590 --> 00:07:00.120
business book that said that the best way

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:04.070
to market a product is to
create a psychological trigger

00:07:04.070 --> 00:07:06.530
that makes people need your product.

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:09.080
The example used in the
book was this toothpaste

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:12.660
in like the '50s or '60s where
the ad for this toothpaste

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:16.060
called attention to this
quote dangerous coating

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:18.530
that robs the teeth of their whiteness.

00:07:18.530 --> 00:07:21.150
Like this film coating
that's on your teeth

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:22.040
every time you eat,

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:23.610
and it's like dangerous and bad

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:24.850
and socially unacceptable.

00:07:24.850 --> 00:07:27.770
Turns out that this
dangerous film on your teeth

00:07:27.770 --> 00:07:30.290
is a harmless residue
from food consumption,

00:07:30.290 --> 00:07:31.670
and toothpaste doesn't remove it

00:07:31.670 --> 00:07:33.620
any better than eating an apple.

00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:35.520
So yes you should
totally brush your teeth,

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:37.850
but not because there's
this dangerous residue,

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:39.840
and now I can't unfeel it.

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:41.670
The psychological
trigger is just baked in,

00:07:41.670 --> 00:07:43.380
I can't not feel it and I feel judged

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:45.090
because I maybe have
this dangerous coating.

00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:46.710
This same dynamic happens today

00:07:46.710 --> 00:07:49.960
with the 100 billion
dollar hair care industry.

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:52.320
They push all sorts of scary ideas

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:55.050
about dirty things lurking in your hair

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:56.940
that only their product can fix.

00:07:56.940 --> 00:07:58.920
And they get very rich because of it.

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:00.570
Telling you that you
have grease in your hair

00:08:00.570 --> 00:08:03.500
makes you feel dirty psychologically.

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:05.050
And what it does is it turns these

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:09.080
naturally occurring lipids,
or fats in your hair

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:11.640
which are totally protective
and naturally occurring

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:14.770
into this gross feeling dangerous thing.

00:08:14.770 --> 00:08:16.780
And more and more these commercials

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:19.410
have these like fancy 3-D diagrams

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:22.070
to make it feel totally legit and medical.

00:08:22.070 --> 00:08:23.610
There are medical things here

00:08:23.610 --> 00:08:26.690
like dandruff is a real skin disorder,

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:28.550
that's something that has real symptoms

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:32.280
and should be treated
in a real medical way

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:33.260
by a professional.

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:36.140
Not by a commercial with a fake doctor

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:38.960
showing you 3-D diagrams
to sell a product.

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:42.270
And no, this lady is not a
legit doctor, she's an actor.

00:08:42.270 --> 00:08:44.810
While we're on the point of
dandruff and itchy scalps,

00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:47.020
let it be known that dry scalp,

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:48.620
which is not a skin disorder,

00:08:48.620 --> 00:08:50.260
literally means that you don't have enough

00:08:50.260 --> 00:08:52.990
hydration in your scalp, is not dandruff.

00:08:52.990 --> 00:08:55.560
- But he's scratching his
head, could be dandruff.

00:08:55.560 --> 00:08:58.720
- And yet they share
effectively the same symptoms,

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:01.870
itchy, flaky, but dry
scalp, unlike dandruff,

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:05.110
is caused in part by, wait for it,

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:07.130
shampooing too much.

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:09.110
Drying out your scalp by stripping it

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:10.900
of its natural hydrating oils.

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:12.350
This was my problem in my 20s.

00:09:12.350 --> 00:09:15.440
I didn't have dandruff,
I thought I had dandruff

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:17.200
because I was shampooing my hair too much

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:18.500
and it was drying out my scalp

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:19.990
and making it dry and flaky.

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:21.200
All of this gets conflated

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:23.740
when corporations present
their advertisements

00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:27.280
as legit science that's meant
to help you feel better.

00:09:27.280 --> 00:09:29.040
But let's just quickly say it like it is,

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:30.170
the only thing they're doing

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:32.400
is trying to sell you a product

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:33.660
to make sure that you feel like

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:35.530
you need it as much as possible.

00:09:35.530 --> 00:09:38.490
Where this becomes totally
below the belt in my view

00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:40.410
is when these commercials tell the story

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:43.020
of how you will be socially ostracized

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:44.390
if you don't use their product.

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:46.480
- [Narrator] Use Head
and Shoulders every day.

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:48.730
- And this gets to the last
point I wanna make here,

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:51.720
and potentially the biggest
reason why I made this video.

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:54.060
I don't are about you
shampooing your hair,

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:57.450
you probably should, you need
to determine that on your own,

00:09:57.450 --> 00:09:58.890
but let us just recognize

00:09:58.890 --> 00:10:00.670
that we are social animals.

00:10:00.670 --> 00:10:03.420
We live and die by what
others think of us.

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:07.150
We strive to be accepted
by the group at any cost.

00:10:07.150 --> 00:10:08.220
And my big fear here

00:10:08.220 --> 00:10:10.760
is that we have given the power

00:10:10.760 --> 00:10:12.920
of what we need to do to be accepted

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:15.950
to these big corporations,
these giant machines

00:10:15.950 --> 00:10:18.510
who use this psychological dynamic

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:20.720
to sell us more of their stuff.

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:22.970
They have successfully turned hair

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:26.470
into a discussion of
hygiene and cleanliness,

00:10:26.470 --> 00:10:28.480
and now we talk about this

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:30.680
almost as a form of epidemiology.

00:10:30.680 --> 00:10:33.260
Cleanliness and hygiene turns into

00:10:33.260 --> 00:10:34.860
an issue of health and safety,

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:37.200
which let's be honest,
brushing your teeth,

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:38.840
or washing your hands,

00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:42.060
that stuff is there to stop
us from spreading diseases.

00:10:42.060 --> 00:10:43.750
I haven't washed my hair in five years

00:10:43.750 --> 00:10:46.640
and there's not some virus
that's gonna pop off my head

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:49.300
and go infect my family.

00:10:49.300 --> 00:10:52.610
Oh that's a very strange
image, head virus.

00:10:52.610 --> 00:10:54.620
There are real skin disorders

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:55.560
having to do with the scalp,

00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:57.490
those should be treated seriously.

00:10:57.490 --> 00:11:00.240
But my sense is that we've conflated that.

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:02.750
We're not talking about
health and disease prevention

00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:03.690
a lot of the time.

00:11:03.690 --> 00:11:07.170
We're talking about beauty
and self-perception.

00:11:07.170 --> 00:11:11.320
That's not epidemiology,
that's personal psychology,

00:11:11.320 --> 00:11:14.770
personal self-esteem,
and societal standards.

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:17.950
That feeling of being dirty or greasy,

00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:19.480
who determined that feeling?

00:11:19.480 --> 00:11:21.900
Who set the parameters for that feeling?

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:24.560
It's not nature, it's not epidemiology.

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:26.160
If you had been born 50 years ago,

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:29.040
you wouldn't have that same
feeling of being greasy.

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:30.020
It's not natural.

00:11:30.020 --> 00:11:32.850
And even in 2021, if
you were born in Spain,

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:35.290
you would less likely have that feeling

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:36.870
of just being dirty

00:11:36.870 --> 00:11:39.970
that drives you to consume more
and more of these products.

00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:42.850
Which helps you build the
nearly 100 billion dollar

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:44.100
hair care industry,

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:46.960
a huge portion of which is
owned by just three companies.

00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:49.680
L'Oreal, Proctor and Gamble, and Unilever

00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:52.440
which find a million ways to feel like

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:55.030
you are dirty, you are undesirable,

00:11:55.030 --> 00:11:56.730
and if you don't use their product,

00:11:56.730 --> 00:11:58.460
you will be ostracized from society.

00:11:58.460 --> 00:12:00.133
Just look at these commercials.

00:12:05.830 --> 00:12:08.280
These companies have cracked
the code on what drives us,

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:10.660
and it's fear and a desire to be accepted.

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:12.030
And this isn't just with hair,

00:12:12.030 --> 00:12:14.370
this is with a million of these products

00:12:14.370 --> 00:12:16.180
that tell us that we're inferior.

00:12:16.180 --> 00:12:19.750
And if I'm saying this
as a man in this society,

00:12:19.750 --> 00:12:22.170
it is a thousand times worse for women.

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:24.540
So am I here telling you
not to shampoo your hair?

00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:26.350
No, do whatever you want.

00:12:26.350 --> 00:12:28.400
You have a totally different
hair experience than I do.

00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:30.650
I'm sure stopping cold turkey like I did

00:12:30.650 --> 00:12:32.010
probably isn't the right choice for you,

00:12:32.010 --> 00:12:35.280
all I'm asking you is to
scrutinize your standards,

00:12:35.280 --> 00:12:37.550
and who is in control of the narrative

00:12:37.550 --> 00:12:40.230
of what clean even means?

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:42.400
Okay, that's that.

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:45.730
Speaking of the psychology of self-esteem

00:12:45.730 --> 00:12:47.650
in the 21st century,

00:12:47.650 --> 00:12:50.220
I wanna tell you about the
sponsor of today's video

00:12:50.220 --> 00:12:51.520
which is Better Help.

00:12:51.520 --> 00:12:53.170
It's an online tool

00:12:53.170 --> 00:12:55.020
that allows you to connect with

00:12:55.020 --> 00:12:56.800
a professional trained counselor

00:12:56.800 --> 00:12:59.460
so that you can have
therapy, but do it remotely.

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:01.800
I've been in therapy for
the past year and a half,

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:04.440
and for the majority of
that it's been remote,

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:06.580
I haven't been sitting in
the therapist's office.

00:13:06.580 --> 00:13:08.460
And I can't stress enough how important

00:13:08.460 --> 00:13:11.200
it has been for me, my
understanding of myself,

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:14.010
and my well-being as a person,

00:13:14.010 --> 00:13:16.330
and as a husband, and as a father,

00:13:16.330 --> 00:13:18.150
and as a brother, and as all the roles

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:19.120
that I play in my life,

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:20.960
therapy has been amazing.

00:13:20.960 --> 00:13:23.070
Better Help is not a crisis line,

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:24.630
it is not a self-help scheme,

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:28.100
it is a platform for finding a counselor

00:13:28.100 --> 00:13:30.250
and starting therapy so that you can

00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:32.360
start to make strides
in your mental health.

00:13:32.360 --> 00:13:33.990
My favorite part about Better Help

00:13:33.990 --> 00:13:36.590
is that it makes it free and easy

00:13:36.590 --> 00:13:38.150
to change your counselors.

00:13:38.150 --> 00:13:39.740
It often takes a while to find

00:13:39.740 --> 00:13:41.690
the right therapist for your life.

00:13:41.690 --> 00:13:44.150
With Better Help you
have a ton of options,

00:13:44.150 --> 00:13:45.660
as well as the ability to,

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:47.850
if you don't find a good fit,

00:13:47.850 --> 00:13:49.330
at first or second or third

00:13:49.330 --> 00:13:50.260
